# Utilities

Command-line tools built on DDS (not API demos).

## `dd_table_for_deal`

Print the double-dummy table and par for a deal from the CLI or a PBN file.

```bash
bazelisk run //utilities:dd_table_for_deal -- hands/example.pbn
bazelisk run //utilities:dd_table_for_deal -- --vul ns hands/example.pbn
bazelisk run //utilities:dd_table_for_deal -- --limit 3 hands/multi_board.pbn
bazelisk test //utilities:dd_table_for_deal_test
```

Python counterpart: `//python/utilities:dd_table_for_deal`.

C++ sources: `utilities/src/dd_table_for_deal/`.

## Hand-list scripts

```bash
bazelisk run //python/utilities:create_list_for_dtest -- -n 100 --seed 100 -o /tmp/list100.txt
./utilities/src/regenerate_hand_lists.sh
./utilities/src/verify_lists.sh hands/list1.txt
```

These rebuild and verify `hands/listN.txt` inputs for `dtest`.
